  "preamble": "The shift from the voiced alveolar/dental stop [d] to the voiced dental fricative [ð] is a textbook example of spirantization and lenition. It occurs very frequently when the stop is placed between two vowels, causing it to weaken and allow continuous airflow. Albanian spirantized intervocalic Proto-Albanian *d to dh [ð] (*skeuda > hedh 'to throw').",
